# Settings for running lmx from this source checkout. Copy this file to .env
# and uncomment the lines you fill in. Never commit a filled-in .env.
#
# Who reads it: `mise exec -- mix lmx ...` and `mix lmx.tui` load the
# checkout's own .env when they start (req_llm does, from the directory
# Mix runs in, whatever -C points the session at), and a variable already
# set in your shell wins over the file. The example scripts that say
# `set -a; . ./.env; set +a` read it too. The installed lmx reads no .env
# file: export these in your shell instead, or paste a key into the panel
# the terminal UI opens when it starts without one, which saves it in
# ~/.lmx/config.json.
#
# Model providers. When nothing names a model (--model, LMX_MODEL, or
# "model" in ~/.lmx/config.json), lmx starts on the model you last chose
# with one of those, if it can still be reached, and otherwise on the
# recommended model of the first provider below whose key is set;
# `lmx help models` lists each one's model. With no key at all it uses a
# model a running Ollama serves that can call tools (start Ollama with
# OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH set to 32768 or more, 65536 recommended), or the
# terminal UI asks you to pick a provider. Leave a key's line commented
# unless you fill it in: an empty value switches off a key saved in
# ~/.lmx/config.json.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# ZAI_API_KEY=
#
# Name a model yourself (PROVIDER:MODEL); a flag still wins over it.
# LMX_MODEL=openai:gpt-6-sol
#
# At most this many model requests per session.
# LMX_MAX_REQUESTS=20
#
# 0 never starts the MCP servers a repository's .mcp.json declares.
# LMX_PROJECT_MCP=0
#
# Web search. Setting a Brave Search key turns web search and page fetching
# on; LMX_WEB_SEARCH=none keeps them off with the key set.
# BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=
# LMX_WEB_SEARCH=none
